  "v": 1,
  "name": "killrecovery-repeat",
  "notes": [
    "TEMPORARY (#1315): drop this file and ios.yml's 'L3 kill-recovery repeat' step when #1315",
    "closes, or on a later ruling.",
    "Fifteen walks of lifecycle.json's kill-recovery phase. Each phase is a fresh relaunch with",
    "-OBInjectFailure killOnce (one simulated content-process death after first readiness, then",
    "the shell's reload), followed by that phase's two interactive-again waits. On main b97e65a8",
    "(ios run 44757799313) WebKit's content process stopped answering after that reload while",
    "-OBDeadBootDiag YES was on. ShellSeam.launchArgs now leaves the flag off any launch that",
    "injects a failure, so every walk here runs without it.",
    "Not carried over from lifecycle: the settings assert and the language reset (they need its",
    "first phase) and the 'recovered' checkpoint (an L4 rendezvous). GestureDriver stops at the",
    "first failing phase."
  ],
  "source": "ios/tools/scenarios/lifecycle.json, phase kill-recovery",
  "viewport": { "width": 844, "height": 390 },
  "boot": { "query": "obtool&norec&seed=1", "ephemeralStore": true, "statusSeam": true },
